cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EffluxScope: a computational framework for evaluating ABCB1 efflux predictors under chemical-space shift"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying
  paper. The reference panel shipped with the ABCB1 instance has its own
  sources, which must be cited independently -- see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/tommyverygood/EffluxScope"
abstract: >-
  EffluxScope is a computational framework for evaluating ABCB1 efflux
  predictors under chemical-space shift. Its endpoint-agnostic core records
  and hashes the decision rules, stratifies a query set by structure-only
  distance to a reference set, compares a candidate abstention rule with the
  evaluated model's own confidence at matched coverage, and evaluates
  pre-declared gates that can return not_evaluable. Reports distinguish rules
  fixed before scoring from exploratory analyses. The software ships one
  worked instance covering ABCB1/P-glycoprotein efflux risk. This is not a
  property predictor; the model bundles it redistributes are objects of
  evaluation in the accompanying paper and
  declare themselves development artefacts.
keywords:
  - model evaluation
  - applicability domain
  - selective prediction
  - abstention
  - distribution shift
  - chemical-space shift
  - coverage-matched evaluation
  - ABCB1
  - P-glycoprotein
